---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/16-03/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Precision steel laboratory bench" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Place a tray on reusable bench anchors and verify its drawer-relative pose."><script is:inline>window.steelModule=import('/equipment/16-03/bench.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="steel-bench"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-03/">← Equipment 16-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#sb-proof">Verification</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">16-03 / WORKSHOP FURNITURE</p><h2>A tray that stays in its drawer</h2><p class="eq-lede">Store Tray A in an open drawer, then close it. Its ID and drawer-relative pose stay fixed even though its position in the room moves 340 mm.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / FURNITURE</p><h3>BTS Steel 1800</h3><div id="sb-view" aria-label="Interactive steel laboratory bench and cream cabinets"></div><small id="sb-model" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</small><div class="tools"><button id="sb-full">Whole bench</button><button id="sb-detail">Drawer detail</button><button id="sb-top">Work surface</button></div><p>The virtual drawer handle and trays are clickable. While holding a tray, select a highlighted open slot or use the explicit placement buttons. Pointer input uses snap targets, not physics-driven dragging.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / PLACEMENT</p><h3>Move and store</h3><p id="sb-state"></p><button id="sb-drawer" class="run">Open drawer</button><div class="tools"><button data-grab="TRAY_A">Grab tray A</button><button data-grab="TRAY_B">Grab tray B</button><button data-grab="CASE_C">Grab wide case C</button></div><div class="tools"><button data-slot="drawer">Place in drawer</button><button data-slot="left">Place left</button><button data-slot="right">Place right</button><button data-slot="side">Place rear</button></div><p id="sb-status" role="status">Ready.</p><button id="sb-reset">Reset positions</button><p>Try case C in the empty drawer: it is 90 mm too wide after margins. Then stow A and try B in the same slot: it fits geometrically but the occupied slot rejects a second object.</p></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / LIVE STATE</p><h3>Anchor occupancy and moving frames</h3><p id="sb-info" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Anchor ID</th><th>Occupant</th><th>Interior W × H × D</th></tr></thead><tbody id="sb-rows"></tbody></table></div><button id="sb-save">Export anchor map JSON</button></section>
<section id="sb-proof"><p class="eq-meta">04 / BASIS & VERIFICATION</p><h3>Designed dimensions and explicit clearance</h3><p>This original furniture design follows the catalogue’s proposed 1,800 × 750 × 900 mm width/depth/top height. Cream storage, steel worktop, open tube framing, levelling feet and cable grommets are authored geometry. There is no measured vendor equivalent. The active drawer is a prismatic model with 340 mm adopted travel; the other cabinet doors and drawers are appearance only.</p><p>The model permits one object per anchor. Box dimensions must fit with 5 mm clearance on each horizontal side and above, independently. Grab removes the prior attachment; placement attaches to the anchor. The drawer root moves on +Z toward the operator while the child local origin is unchanged. This does not test structural capacity, swing/swept collision, tipping, real runner travel, electrical grounding or egress. It does not change the saved virtual lab design.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Independent case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Verified</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>A in drawer, close-and-open cycle</th><td>Same identity and local pose; 340 mm world movement</td><td>Pass · exact identity and pose; distance within 10⁻⁹ m</td></tr><tr><th>A and B target same anchor</th><td>Reject B; A unchanged</td><td>Pass</td></tr><tr><th>Case C in empty drawer</th><td>90 mm width deficit</td><td>Pass · within 10⁻⁹ m</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The <code>bts.lab-bench-anchors.v1</code> export stores bench and stable object IDs, state revision, occupied/free anchors and local/world metre poses. The scene is floor-centred, +Y up and +Z toward the operator. Consumers can use the drawer and anchor pose API directly in VR. No physical headset session is claimed.</p><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'steel-bench.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry checks and VR targets</a><a href={p+'bench.mjs'}>Anchor/attachment API</a><a href={p+'example-anchors.json'}>Example closed-drawer scene</a></div></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-03/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#steel-bench .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.13fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#steel-bench section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}#steel-bench .cols section{margin:0}#steel-bench .eq-meta{margin:0}#steel-bench h3{margin:.3rem 0 .65rem;font-size:1.5rem}#steel-bench .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.44rem;margin:.65rem 0}#steel-bench button{min-height:40px;padding:.4rem;max-width:100%;font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);background:var(--panel,transparent);cursor:pointer}#steel-bench button.run{background:#345e53;color:white}#sb-view{height:clamp(265px,32vw,410px);background:#293637}#sb-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#steel-bench .over{overflow:auto;margin:.7rem 0}#steel-bench table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#steel-bench th,#steel-bench td{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#sb-info{font-weight:bold}#steel-bench code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){#steel-bench .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#steel-bench section{padding:.65rem}}
</style>
